mechanism:
v13 funnel (v13/DESIGN.md §3, HANDOFF.md). Every model step ran on Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5, via `claude -p`, no tools, one call; output could come in parts through ===== CONTINUE =====). Effort was high, with arms at xhigh and max. Records are in English; only the prose is Turkish.

Step 0, packet.py (script). Per window (short surah = one window, otherwise the pericope ±7), window.md holds:
- the window text;
- "the scan": every branch of every root in the window as `Bnnn gloss | image`;
- the channel-review excerpt.

Per ayah:
- ayah.md: QAC words, anchor translation, word notes from V9 context.md;
- dictionary.md: focus roots, one line per branch with gloss | image | definition | first classical phrase;
- pairs.md: V9 script image partners (same / ±7 / surah), ranked by reciprocal-rank affinity (v9/prepare.py:212-222);
- concordance.md: roots with ≤60 uses, every use with its clause;
- hft.md;
- reciprocal.md.

Measured sizes: S1 window.md 63 KB, 18:76-105 window.md 156 KB; per-ayah hft.md 25-62 KB (the largest per-ayah file); 18:96 step-1 input compacted from 594 KB to 350 KB (DESIGN §8).

Step 1, act (Opus). Discovery stance, no pruning and no verdicts. Output is F-records: `kind | words | branches | trigger (scope) | with | image | anchor | memory`, with 12 kinds (local, window, surah, chain, loaded, cross-definition, concept, scene, fragment, loss, grammar). The first run produced 31-66 records per ayah (v13/out/test1.run.log).

Step N, net (Opus, per surah). Assembles the I-images with members, roles, movement, meetings and purpose, plus a disclosure plan (meet / touch / develop / assemble). Members found in the scan are marked N-added, and unabsorbed findings are listed as `unplaced`. S1 produced 15, 25, 23 and 28 images in four runs (my count).

Step 2, qeq (Opus). Per finding: supports / expands / shifts / contradicts, with [staging] and [same-word] tags; new Q findings (the fourth scope); an A axis pass. References only, from the model's own knowledge of the Quran (prompts/qeq.md).

Step 3, write (Opus). Turkish prose plus a coverage block. Its inputs changed across arms:
- first run: ayah, act, qeq, full network, dictionary, branches (149 KB for 1:6);
- v2: added mustland.md, the must-land obligation list (49-144 items);
- v3: mustland became a ranked budget (≤2 assemblies), plus window_text, previous.md (the prior ayah's prose, written sequentially), concordance and variants;
- v4: network.view.md, passages attached per job, axis set; 235 KB input for 1:6.

Step S (surah prose) was never built. Script checks: record ids, branch existence (unknown_branches = [] in every act.check.json), and verify_src exact-tag verification with at most one repair.

v14 (v14/DESIGN.md, STABILIZATION.md, ARGUMENT_TRIAL.md). Upstream was frozen from v13 v2 (act, QeQ and network for 1:6); v14's act/net/qeq prompts are the v13 v2-era copies (13:26/14:09 timestamps). The components:
- synthesis.py builds a "lossless" index (every F, E_F, Q, A, image and meeting record; 95 KB for 1:6, 192 items).
- The writer gets write.md, ayah, window_text, synthesis.md, dictionary, branches, concordance, variants and the full previous 1:5 prose (49 KB). Total 201-207 KB, plus the lookup helper (sources.py; exact verifier spelling; ≤16 refs plus 0-3 neighbours per query; logged in source.lookups.jsonl).
- The writer returns prose plus a trace JSON. Schema 1 copied whole paragraphs (51.4% of output). Schema 2 used short anchors. Schema 3 has links, partial and deferred rows, with no quality grades.
- review.py adds a frozen, evaluation-only regression gate (10, then 15 passage criteria), independent review JSONs and an immutable accept pointer (never created).
- External writers used export → exclusive claim → one agent → ingest, with gpt-6-sol and gpt-6-astra at max effort and no token or billing data.

The 29:38 blind run: fresh Opus-high act+QeQ ($4.41), then one Astra writer, with no window network and no previous prose.

The composition trial (composition.py, prompts/compose.md, write_composition.md):
1. Sol reads the full research (171,674 bytes plus 6 lookups) and returns an integrated explanation and evidence selection in JSON (819 words; 19 of 169 records selected).
2. A fresh Astra writes the prose from a 66,379-byte selected packet and made 0 lookups.

The primary agent reviewed everything; no comparison agents were used.

inputs_pulled_or_optional:
v14 lookup helper (sources.py; `--source-mode lookup`): exact Quran passages plus 0-3 neighbouring ayat, logged in source.lookups.jsonl. Measured pulls:
